  "privacyHeading": "Your Copies, Your Privacy",
  "privacyTitle": "Your photos always belong to you.",
  "privacyBody": "Your photos go to a bucket you own, as ordinary files. Alongside them sits an index.csv listing every photo by date, album, person, caption and place — so you can find any one of them again with a spreadsheet and nothing else. No account, no export tool, no us. This app has no permission to delete from your bucket; only you do.\n\nNothing is ever sent to the developer. There is no server and no account: your library, its records and its face data stay in a database on this iPhone, and all processing — grouping, search, face recognition — happens here. Photos go only where you send them: your own bucket, your own iCloud, your own AI key. Keys are kept in the Keychain and are never included in a backup.",
